From: Firmware Security Follow-up <security@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi ibss own bss reference in joined event

Complete upstream event representation, early referenced lookup, allocation-failure put, event reference transfer, and all consumer early-return puts. Adapt kzalloc_obj to the existing kzalloc(sizeof(*ev), gfp) allocator. Teardown already processes the complete event queue via cfg80211_process_wdev_events; retain that path and both WEXT and nl80211 notifications.

CVE: CVE-2026-98338
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/708f9d43d6a2eb9c6b83fe62af628de9dffd9314]

